within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.B_BloodAndBloodFormingOrgans.B01A_AntithromboticAgents.B01AA03_Warfarin;
model Warfarin "Warfarin — default model: Warfarin_NeffDavis1981_reference"
  extends Warfarin_NeffDavis1981_reference;
  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>The default model of warfarin: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.B_BloodAndBloodFormingOrgans.B01A_AntithromboticAgents.B01AA03_Warfarin.Warfarin_NeffDavis1981_reference\">Warfarin_NeffDavis1981_reference</a>, chosen among the models extracted from papers (reviewer verdict, ground-truth agreement, completeness). All models of warfarin in this package:</p><ul><li><code>Warfarin_Aoyama2022_reference</code></li><li><code>Warfarin_Hirai2024_prior_values</code></li><li><code>Warfarin_Mungall1985_reference</code></li><li><code>Warfarin_NeffDavis1981_reference</code></li><li><code>Warfarin_Yuen2010_reference</code></li><li><code>Warfarin_Zhu2017_reference</code></li></ul><h4>About warfarin</h4><p>Warfarin is an anticoagulant used to prevent and treat blood clots in conditions such as atrial fibrillation, heart valve disease, pulmonary embolism, thrombosis, and heart disease. It is widely used in human medicine and is included on the WHO list of essential medicines, though it also serves as a rodenticide and carries a boxed warning.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q113368879\">Wikidata Q113368879</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Warfarin\">Warfarin</a>.</p></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>10/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from default: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: default</li></ul></body></html>"), experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 345600, Tolerance = 1e-9, Interval = 1));
end Warfarin;
